<title>UK: Sema half year pretax profit surges.</title>
<headline>Sema half year pretax profit surges.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		13.23		  vs 10.47</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.3		    vs 1.9</p>
<p> Pretax		     19.75		  vs 15.2</p>
<p> Turnover		   426.9		  vs 321.9</p>
<p>NOTE - UK informational technology firm Sema Group said its total order book had strengthened 31 percent to 991 million stg since the end of 1995 and it looked forward to the future with confidence.Sema said its strong organic growth, development of new technologies and strategic acquisitions had helped results.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 21.18		  vs 15.90</p>
<p> Interest		   1.43 payable	 vs 0.13 receivable</p>
<p> Tax charge		 5.01		   vs 3.59</p>
<p> Net taxed		  14.72		  vs 11.62</p>
<p> Retained profit	  10.26		  vs 8.06</p>
<p> Pay date		   Nov 1</p>
<p>Div registration date  Oct 1  Ex-div date		Sept 23</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
